[] [] [textBox1] You’ve almost completed the tutorials! Next technique involves “Naked Pairs”.
[] [] [textBox2] A naked pair is when you have exactly two cells within a row, column, or 3×3 block that only have the exact same two candidates
[] [] [textBox3] When this happens, you know where the digits that form the pair go, just don’t know which order they go in. 
[] [] [textBox1] Similarly to hidden pairs, this means that you can eliminate all other candidate pairs from the row/column/box
[] [] [textBox2] There is one naked pair somewhere in this puzzle. Click the two cells that make up the naked pair.
[] [] [textBox3] Great! Using this technique is a great way to keep the puzzle organized.
[] [] [textBox1] You’ve reached the end of the tutorials. Click practice to try out a puzzle on your own! You can also revisit any tutorial by clicking ‘Tutorials’.

Two cells are 2 numbers